# ER (exact resume P0, docs/tp4-exact-resume.md 5.2): a committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a
# throwaway commit of tp4/exact-resume and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-er-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-er-1/<tag>/' *.env). The twins (-fx-all-er, -fx-all-er-audit) are
# placed in qwen_c2_profiles.json by WP0 from scripts/ci/fusion-wp/ER.json (make_fusion_profiles.py --write); until then the templates naming them do not pass c2_serving_job.py's profile check.
# The cards serve production: the owner stops the node agent and unserves production BEFORE X0 and restores it after Z (the cutover pack's steps and post-checks); nothing here does either.
# B0 (STOP): the window image, built from the pushed branch head with the production profile baked as the serving default (the same default production runs, so the image could serve); the
# gate-only twins are in its profiles file and the window selects them per job. READ: 'baking the serving default c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic with a session cap of 8', the
# provenance report with no problem line (the overlay carries scripts/ci/prefix_window_carry.py and the plugin copies of qwen_prefix_registry.py and qwen_prefix_scheduler_patch.py), the image id.
# A build, not a card job. Duration (estimate): 40 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-er-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
